### Control Interface / Triggers (CITv2)
* **Presentation**: [CITv2 IETF 127](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-cdni-citv2-ietf-127-00) presented by Alan.
* **Draft Updates (`draft-ietf-cdni-ci-triggers-rfc8007bis`)**:
  * **Error Handling Refactoring**: Immediate rejection via synchronous HTTP status codes (4xx/5xx) is required if an error is known at trigger creation time. Asynchronous error reporting is reserved strictly for errors emerging later during processing or across cascaded CDNs.
  * **Error Payload**: Introduced payload type `application/cdni.ci.trigger-error.v2+json` (`CI.TriggerError.v2`) so that synchronous rejections downstream can be passed asynchronously upstream when needed.
  * **Trigger Filtering**: Unified filtering using a JSON object structure for trigger labels (matching paradigms like Kubernetes) rather than flat string key-value parsing. Filtering by state remains mandatory, while individual label-based filter collections are optional for downstream CDNs (dCDNs).
  * **Capability & Status Fixes**: Restructured FCI capabilities, clarified error codes (400 for bad requests, 501 for unsupported operations), and aligned extended status enforcement.
* **Publication Readiness**: Authors requested moving to Working Group Last Call (WGLC) once shepherd and chair reviews are complete.

